SRC/ag2 -- ag, the anagram generator, as built for OS-9/68000=============================================================ORIG holds the post as comp.sources.games carried it, less pref.c: that wasits author's lex output, which contains lex's own driver code; pref.l, thesource it came from, is there.  anagram.c differs from the post in oneplace, under #ifdef OSK: its default word list is /dd/GAMES/words, the onethis disk carries, instead of /usr/dict/words.  -d still names another.Only ag is built.  Sean Barrett's two filters, pref.l and postf.c, publicdomain, tune a Unix dictionary for anagramming; GAMES/words already holdsonly lower-case words, so they are kept in ORIG and not built.